      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the speaker's self-identification through the meme's text and imagery",
      "description": "The user is projecting themselves onto the speaker of the meme, who is claiming to be 'not a gay SJW like other femboys' and 'racist and a gamer, daddy uwu'. The projection is onto the textual material and the visual materials (woman and dog) that represent the speaker's self-identification. The text explicitly uses 'im' (first person singular), which directly projects the user as the speaker. The visual materials (woman and dog) are used as proxies for the speaker's identity, which the user is adopting or identifying with.",
